          %h2#examples_and_applications Examples and applications
          %h3#univalent_tarski_universes Univalent Tarski universes
          %p
            Tarski universes are types which behave like internal models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            inside of the type theory itself. We use a very general notion of Tarski universe: a Tarski universe merely consists of a type of encodings for types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            and a universal type family
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒯
                      %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}_\mathcal{U}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:\mathcal{U}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a function
